WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.502 --> 00:00:05.040
[Upbeat music playing]

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.134
Here we are sharing a meal like we are used to&nbsp;
doing so very often in our daily lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:15.520
But what we might not always realize is that along with&nbsp;
our own efforts at preparing the various foods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:21.120
other living entities play hugely important roles&nbsp;
in making the foods we serve not only edible but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.354
nutritious and simply delicious. 

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.360
These living&nbsp;
entities we do not normally perceive as being&nbsp;alive.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.800
These are the microbes that over millennia&nbsp;
have transformed many ingredients turning them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:40.876
into such delightful food and drink as bread&nbsp;
cheese, beer, and wine and many many others.

00:00:40.876 --> 00:00:46.000
So for thousands and thousands of years humans&nbsp;
have been taking advantage of microbial growth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.878
to ferment and preserve their foods. 

00:00:49.878 --> 00:00:51.878
But&nbsp; it is not all just about food preservation,

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.240
fermented foods are safe to eat but they can also&nbsp;
provide entirely new textures and flavors making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.531
them thoroughly enjoyable to consume.

00:01:00.531 --> 00:01:03.469
So welcome&nbsp;to the marvelous world of microbial foods.

